# UR3Pick sweep — DRY: base config lives in manipulation_params.py (PPO) +
# ur3_pick.py default_config() (env). Each line below carries ONLY per-run
# metadata plus the knob(s) that actually vary; every omitted key inherits the
# baked base_polar best-known defaults (30M steps, num_evals=40,
# num_resets_per_eval=1, gamma=0.99, LR=6e-4, reward_scaling=0.05 -> TOTAL~31.9M;
# action_scale=0.015, action_rate=-0.10, gripper=0.02, init_start_random=mid).
# Reproducibility is preserved because run_experiment logs full_cfg + git_commit.
# Comment/blank lines are skipped by the runner and do NOT count toward the
# 1-based SLURM_ARRAY_TASK_ID.
#
# Domain-randomization ABLATION: layer ONE physics-DR axis at a time (LIGHT band)
# on top of the known-good config (the Smooth_slow_mid_as015_ar10 winner, now
# baked) at episode_length=400, to see how each axis trains vs a no-DR baseline.
# episode_length is a rollout truncation, NOT a step multiplier, so every line is
# still ~31.9M steps. DR knobs are nested config passed via dotted keys, which
# run_experiment forwards to registry.load (see the domain_rand block in
# ur3_pick.py). Line 1 is the no-DR control (reproduces the winner at ep400).
{"env_name": "UR3Pick", "seed": 1, "run_id": "DR_baseline_ep400", "wandb_project": "UR3_pick_ppo", "video_every_evals": 6, "render_every": 1, "episode_length": 400, "wandb_tags": ["DR", "ablation", "baseline", "noDR", "ep400", "s1"]}
